    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess, but that \"significance\" feels so temporary and forced. like we're just pretending. if the physics say it's all just a slow slide into nothingness, then all this effort to stay positive or \"find meaning\" feels like fighting a losing battle against the math. isn't there a certain logic to just accepting the entropy? instead of wasting all this energy to keep a flame lit that's destined to go out anyway?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
